  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc, which outperforms the best RNA-only multiprofile (config_006, 0.653 acc) by ~3.5 pp, suggesting the image modality adds modest but real value. However, we have only one multimodal data point and have not yet isolated the effect of the fusion strategy. Config_033 is identical to config_032 except it uses weighted fusion instead of concat, making it a clean single-variable A/B comparison. This tells us whether the way modalities are combined is a meaningful design lever or whether concat is already near-optimal. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information next step: it either confirms concat is sufficient (freeing us to explore image encoder quality or aggregation next) or reveals that weighted fusion meaningfully improves multimodal performance, guiding subsequent experiments toward better fusion-aware configurations."
}

